node_modules/

# `dist/` is deliberately NOT ignored, and is deliberately tracked. The consuming app
# installs this package straight from GitHub (`github:f3r21/ravn-ui-kit#<tag>`), and a
# git install runs no build: npm clones, looks for a `prepare` script, finds none, and
# packs whatever `package.json`'s `files` names. With `dist/` ignored that tarball ships
# an exports map pointing at four files that are not in it.
#
# The alternative — `"prepare": "npm run build"` — was considered and rejected: it makes
# every consumer install (their CI, every preview deploy, every worktree) pull this
# repo's ~370 MB devDependency tree and run a full build. Committing 340 KB of generated
# output keeps installs as fast as they are today and keeps the build in the repo that
# owns it. `.gitattributes` marks it `linguist-generated -diff` so it does not drown out
# real changes in review, and CI fails when it is stale — never hand-edit it.

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Storybook
storybook-static/
*.local

# Playwright MCP scratch artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code — per-machine session state only. The rest of .claude/ is tracked
# deliberately: settings, hooks and commands must reach every git worktree, and a
# worktree only receives files that are committed. Skills are excluded below
# because corvus manages them and `corvus sync` restores them from .corvusrc.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/statsig/
.claude/todos/

# Internal audit docs — kept local only, not pushed
UI_KIT_MASTER_PLAN.md
MIGRATION_GAPS.md

# `.corvusrc` is deliberately NOT ignored, and is deliberately tracked. It is the
# skill manifest, and a `git worktree` only receives committed files — untrack it
# and every fresh worker session starts with no skills and no way to discover
# which ones this project expects, because `corvus sync` reads the manifest to
# restore them. The skill directories below stay ignored; corvus owns their
# contents. If `corvus install` rewrites the block and re-adds `.corvusrc`, the
# tracking is what matters — delete the line again rather than untracking the file.

# corvus — managed, do not edit this block
.claude/skills/figma-to-react-components/
.claude/skills/design-variations/
.claude/skills/type-system-audit/
.claude/skills/agent-init-deep/
.claude/skills/test-case-gen/
.claude/skills/qa-happy-path/
.claude/skills/qa-bug-fixer/
.claude/skills/core-coding-standards/
.claude/skills/lang-typescript/
.claude/skills/platform-frontend/
.claude/skills/tech-react/
.claude/skills/design-accessibility/
.claude/skills/platform-testing/
.claude/skills/tech-vitest/
.claude/skills/agent-pr-creator/
# end corvus

# Vitest coverage output. Untracked by luck until now — nothing ignored it, so a `git add -A`
# during a rebase swept `coverage-summary.json` into a commit (#98). The reporter is invoked by
# hand when re-deriving numerators for the ratchet, so the directory appears and disappears.
coverage/
